12.1 Language and words (bltzread-bltzr)
========================================

‘bltzread-language’
     Language of this buffer (buffer-local).
‘bltzread-bltzr-executable’, ‘bltzread-bltzr-extra-args’
     The program.
‘bltzread-default-language’, ‘bltzread-detect-sample-size’
     The language when a buffer has none, and how much text is used to
     detect it.
‘bltzread-word-regexp’, ‘bltzread-word-regexp-alist’
     What counts as a word, in general and per language.
‘bltzread-skip-numerals’
     Never mark a token with no letter in it.
‘bltzread-track-by’
     ‘form’ keeps a level for each spelling; ‘lemma’ keeps one level for
     a basic word and all its forms.
‘bltzread-make-read-only’
     Make the buffer read-only while the mode is on.
‘bltzread-reannotate-on-change’
     Read the words again after the text changed: nil never, a number of
     idle seconds, or t.
‘bltzread-tokenizer-function’, ‘bltzread-lemmatizer-function’, ‘bltzread-language-detect-function’
     The three seams to bltzr (see _Extending bltzread_).
‘bltzread-no-colors’, ‘bltzread-no-colors-show-level’
     See _No-colors mode_.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Levels (bltzread-levels),  Next: Skip lists and storage (bltzread-lists),  Prev: Language and words (bltzread-bltzr),  Up: Options

12.2 Levels (bltzread-levels)
=============================

‘bltzread-level-names’, ‘bltzread-level-faces’
     Names and faces of the five levels.
‘bltzread-level-scope’
     ‘word’ (default): setting a level changes every form of the word.
     ‘form’: only that spelling.
‘bltzread-promotion-thresholds’
     Clean reads needed to climb from level 1, 2, 3 and 4.  Default 3 3
     4 5.
‘bltzread-count-each-occurrence’
     Count a word every time it appears in the range, instead of once
     per session.
‘bltzread-lookup-effect’
     What a lookup does: ‘reset-reads’, ‘demote’, or ‘nothing’.
‘bltzread-lookup-counts’, ‘bltzread-lookup-dwell’
     What counts as a lookup (see _The card_).
‘bltzread-unknown-max-level’
     Words at or below this level are "unknown" for the jump keys.
‘bltzread-review-reject-level’
     The level a rejected word drops to.
‘bltzread-undo-limit’
     How many changes ‘bltzread-undo’ can take back.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Skip lists and storage (bltzread-lists),  Next: Card (bltzread-popup),  Prev: Levels (bltzread-levels),  Up: Options

12.3 Skip lists and storage (bltzread-lists)
============================================

‘bltzread-known-write-policy’, ‘bltzread-warn-known-write-unset’
     When known words go to the skip lists.
