15.3.1 Step 1. Read
-------------------

Turn the mode on and read a few paragraphs.  Look up the words you do
not know.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Step 2 Finish the session,  Next: Step 3 Move your bookmark,  Prev: Step 1 Read,  Up: Part 2 Letting bltzread follow your reading

15.3.2 Step 2. Finish the session
---------------------------------

Press ‘s f’.  bltzread asks which part you read.  By default it proposes
everything from the start to the farthest place on screen you reached.
Press Enter to accept.

   You should see a message saying how many words were counted.  Words
you did not look up now have one clean read.  Do this on a few more days
and they climb a level, when they have enough reads.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Step 3 Move your bookmark,  Next: Step 4 If you read everything easily,  Prev: Step 2 Finish the session,  Up: Part 2 Letting bltzread follow your reading

15.3.3 Step 3. Move your bookmark
---------------------------------

After counting, bltzread may ask whether to move the bookmark to where
you stopped.  Say yes to pick up there next time.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Step 4 If you read everything easily,  Next: Step 5 Closing the buffer,  Prev: Step 3 Move your bookmark,  Up: Part 2 Letting bltzread follow your reading

15.3.4 Step 4. If you read everything easily
--------------------------------------------

Press ‘C-u s f’ to count the range and mark all words in it as known.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: Step 5 Closing the buffer,  Next: A warning about books,  Prev: Step 4 If you read everything easily,  Up: Part 2 Letting bltzread follow your reading

15.3.5 Step 5. Closing the buffer
---------------------------------

If you kill the buffer without finishing, bltzread asks whether to
record your reading.  Answer yes and it takes you through the same
steps.


File: bltzread.info,  Node: A warning about books,  Prev: Step 5 Closing the buffer,  Up: Part 2 Letting bltzread follow your reading

15.3.6 A warning about books
----------------------------

In a book opened with nov.el, going to the next chapter replaces the
text.  Finish the session first.


